# Repo Workflow

This is **OmniGame**: a data-driven, pure-functional engine for 2D grid games.
Games are typed JSON configs the engine interprets—not bespoke hardcoding per title.
Live demo: [omnigame.vercel.app](https://omnigame.vercel.app/).

## Documents (different jobs)

| Artifact | Job |
|---|---|
| `README.md` | Durable product vision, architecture, non-goals (primary reference) |
| `docs/semantics.md` | Formal composition / feature-contract semantics (draft; may lag kernel) |
| `docs/scratchpad.md` | **Historical** design notes — not current backlog |
| `PLANNING.md` | Planning & coordination — milestones, marathon runbook, status board |
| `OPEN_ISSUES.md` | Current open work items + acceptance criteria (prioritized) |
| `SCRATCHPAD.json` | Agent session snapshot (focus / next step) |
| `app/` / `src/` | Implementation (Next.js UI + engine/schemas/presets) |
| `references/` | Standalone reference games (design corpus; excluded from tsconfig) |

See the **project-state** rule for write cadences and how continuity files overlap
without replacing each other.

## Stack (orient quickly)

- **App:** Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui
- **Engine:** pure reducers + `GameKernel` in `src/engine/`; Zod in `src/schemas/`
- **Sandbox:** JSON editor + form + Three.js canvas under `app/sandbox/`
- **FP:** Effect.ts (RNG / composition); Zod at JSON edge
- **Optional tooling:** z3-solver (experimental server helper — not sandbox-wired)
- **Package manager:** `pnpm@10.5.2` — Node `>=20.19.0`
- **Verify:** `pnpm install` → `pnpm typecheck` → `pnpm test` (≥289 tests)

## Marathon / cloud agents

Follow `PLANNING.md` marathon runbook and `OPEN_ISSUES.md` P0→Pn order. Prefer
composition honesty before new mechanisms. Mechanism-first reference selection
(project-structure rule).

## Divergence protocol

Never let the prototype and `README.md` (vision) diverge silently. When an
implementation choice improves on or contradicts the documented vision:

1. Implement it (if justified), and
2. Record the mismatch as an `OPEN_ISSUES.md` entry (and/or update `README.md` /
   `docs/semantics.md` if the user asked for a concept change). Plan any phased
   rollout in `PLANNING.md`.
